{% comment %}
  SECTION: Fuel Check Comparison
  Add to Shopify: Online Store → Themes → Edit code → Sections → New section → paste this
  Then add to the betterday page (or homepage) template via the theme editor —
  slots naturally right after Section-Ingredients-Transparency.liquid, since
  it's the same "prove it, don't just claim it" job with a direct comparison.

  Built 2026-09-27 to match the "Fuel Check" social carousel format (weekly
  reference-carousel pillar, see growth_playbooks/visual_winning_pattern_system.md)
  — same underlying data, restyled to the site's existing design system
  (Section-Ingredients-Transparency.liquid's espresso/cream/gold palette)
  rather than importing the carousel's separate navy/cream system. The
  content should travel across platforms; the visual skin follows whatever
  system is already live on each one.

  Numbers: Power Coffee column is the Illuminate Labs certified panel
  (07-Project_info/certifications/README_Illuminate_Labs_Certification.md —
  175mg caffeine, 2.1g taurine, 0g sugar). Red Bull and black coffee columns
  are each brand's own public nutrition label / USDA average — cite the
  source line at the bottom before changing either.
{% endcomment %}

<section class="pc-fuelcheck" id="fuel-check">
  <div class="pc-fuelcheck__inner">

    <div class="pc-fuelcheck__header">
      <span class="pc-fuelcheck__eyebrow">Fuel Check</span>
      <h2 class="pc-fuelcheck__title">Yes, it's in Red Bull too.<br>Here's the actual math.</h2>
      <p class="pc-fuelcheck__subtitle">
        Taurine isn't unique to Power Coffee — Red Bull has it too. The
        difference is the dose, and what it's actually there to do. Same
        honesty as our ingredient panel above: real numbers, not a vibe.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="pc-fuelcheck__table-wrap">
      <table class="pc-fuelcheck__table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th class="pc-fuelcheck__th pc-fuelcheck__th--label"></th>
            <th class="pc-fuelcheck__th pc-fuelcheck__th--us">Power Coffee</th>
            <th class="pc-fuelcheck__th">Red Bull</th>
            <th class="pc-fuelcheck__th">Black Coffee</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td class="pc-fuelcheck__row-label">Caffeine</td>
            <td class="pc-fuelcheck__val pc-fuelcheck__val--us">175mg</td>
            <td class="pc-fuelcheck__val">80mg</td>
            <td class="pc-fuelcheck__val">~95mg</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="pc-fuelcheck__row-label">Taurine</td>
            <td class="pc-fuelcheck__val pc-fuelcheck__val--us">2.1g</td>
            <td class="pc-fuelcheck__val">1g</td>
            <td class="pc-fuelcheck__val">0mg</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="pc-fuelcheck__row-label">Sugar</td>
            <td class="pc-fuelcheck__val pc-fuelcheck__val--us">0g</td>
            <td class="pc-fuelcheck__val">27g</td>
            <td class="pc-fuelcheck__val">0g</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="pc-fuelcheck__note">
      <p class="pc-fuelcheck__note-body">
        Taurine isn't a stimulant — research indicates it functions as a
        neuromodulator, supporting the nervous system's inhibitory response
        rather than adding to the stimulation itself. That's the piece
        missing from "it's just caffeine and sugar" — the taurine is there
        to help keep the caffeine's lift from turning into a jittery spike.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="pc-fuelcheck__footer">
      <p class="pc-fuelcheck__sources">
        Sources: Power Coffee figures per the Illuminate Labs certified panel.
        Caffeine safety threshold: EFSA, 2015 (200mg single-dose). Taurine
        research: Ripps &amp; Shen, <em>Molecular Vision</em>, 2012, and
        endurance-dose research (1–6g range), PubMed 29546641. Red Bull and
        black coffee figures from each product's own published nutrition
        label / USDA average.
      </p>
      <p class="pc-fuelcheck__disclaimer">
        These statements have not been evaluated by the Food and Drug Administration.
        This product is not intended to diagnose, treat, cure, or prevent any disease.
      </p>
    </div>

  </div><!-- /.pc-fuelcheck__inner -->
</section>

